<h2 id="kvo-1">KVO</h2>

<p>We often use KVO in development. Let’s answer KVO-related questions below.</p>

<h3 id="kvo-implementation-principle">KVO implementation principle</h3>

<p>By deriving a subclass via <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">runtime</code>, the properties that need KVO observation are overridden. NSObject’s observation methods are called before and after the setter of that property, so KVO implements callbacks before and after the property change.</p>

<p>The specific format of the subclass derived by KVO should be: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSKVONotifying_ + class name</code>, e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSKVONotifying_Person</code>.</p>

